# Dependencies
node_modules

# Build output
.next
out
dist
.turbo
sdks/rust/target
sdks/go/bin
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target

# Env / secrets (keep .env.example)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.airtable.env
*.pem
*.key

# Key material. A Solana keypair is a plain .json array of 64 bytes, so the
# *.key / *.pem patterns above do NOT catch it — which left the one file that
# controls 1,000,000,000 FURL and the active mint authority a `git add -A` away
# from being committed. Once pushed, a leaked key is public forever; deleting it
# in the next commit changes nothing. These patterns are the backstop.
#
# Keys belong OUTSIDE this repo entirely: this tree is inside OneDrive, so
# anything here is also uploaded to a third party. See C:\Users\ashut\keys.
keys/
**/keys/
*keypair*.json
*-keypair.json
id.json
wallet.json
*.mnemonic
*.seed

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# APK decompilation audits (huge, never deploy)
*-apk/
indmoney-apk/
redotpay-apk/
robinhood-apk/
apktool-output/

# Release binaries (build outputs — 100MB+ each; distribute via Play/CI, never git)
*.apk
*.aab

# Python build artifacts
*.egg-info/

.vercel
.env*
supabase/.temp/

# Local AI-agent session artifacts (never deploy)
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Marketing/media assets — kept out of git history (31MB+ of binaries is
# permanent once committed and cannot be cleanly removed later).
*.mp4
furlpay*.png
wear os*.png

# Lead/prospect data. Contains contact details for real individuals and this
# repo has outside collaborators. Keep it out of version control entirely.
furlpay_prospects_enriched_v2.csv
furlpay_prospects_enriched_v2.xlsx

# Scratch capture of a third-party site, kept locally for analysis only. It
# contains another company's minified bundle and branding, so it must never
# enter this repo's history — committing it would ship their code inside a
# commercial product.
furlpay_pay/

# Cloned capture of tangem.com, kept locally as a design/reference artefact.
# Same reasoning as furlpay_pay/ above: it is another company's markup, minified
# bundles, fonts and branding. It must never enter this repo's history.
reference/

# Product screenshots kept locally for design review. Same reasoning as the
# marketing assets above: multi-MB PNGs are permanent once committed. The
# existing furlpay*.png / wear os*.png rules did not cover these filenames.
/hotels map.png
/portfolio dashboard.png
/portfolio dashboard and wallet.png
/screen app 2 .png
/ticket confirmation screen.png
/trading chart.png

# Scratch scaffolding that rewrites audit/mobile-ux-audit.md from empty.
# Keeping it in the repo invites someone to run it and truncate the audit.
/build_sections.py

# Another company's logo, kept locally as a reference artefact only.
/wikiexpo-lo.svg

# Personal fundraising / founder-community research. Not product material and
# this repo has outside collaborators.
/fintech_founder_opportunities_2026.csv
/stablecoin_funding_investors_2026.csv

# Python virtualenvs. mempool-sentinel/.venv alone is 32MB across 1,868 files;
# a venv is machine-specific and rebuilt from requirements.txt, so committing
# one adds permanent history for something nobody can use.
.venv/
venv/

# Python bytecode. Regenerated on every run and platform-specific.
# NOTE: sdks/python/furlpay/__pycache__/*.pyc are ALREADY tracked and stay
# tracked — .gitignore does not untrack. Removing them is a separate change.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rust build output. furlpay-validator/target is 27MB of compiled artefacts
# rebuilt by `cargo build`. Same reasoning as the media rules above: permanent
# once committed, and worthless to anyone who checks the repo out.
target/

# Product screenshot, same reasoning as the other root PNGs above — the
# existing rules did not cover this filename.
/map.png

# Reference screenshots and scratch images dropped in while working. They are
# inputs to a task, not source: a 1.75MB PNG committed once stays in history
# forever, and none of these are referenced by any code.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.jfif
/*.webp

# Playwright browser-QA artifacts. Screenshots and traces can contain session
# cookies and whatever was on screen, so they never belong in the repo.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Signing material and mobile service configs.
#
# None of these are currently tracked — verified with `git ls-files` during the
# release audit — but nothing stopped the next `git add -A` from committing one.
# A keystore or a .p8 in history cannot be un-published by deleting the file
# later; the key has to be rotated. These rules make the accident impossible
# rather than merely unlikely.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
# App Store Connect / APNs auth keys.
AuthKey_*.p8
*.p8
# Firebase/Google service configs carry project identifiers and client ids, and
# differ per environment — they belong in CI secrets, not in the tree.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
# Gradle signing properties (storePassword / keyAlias live here).
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# Real-Postgres concurrency harness (embedded-postgres data dir, ephemeral)
.pgdata-*

# Local audit evidence scratch (not product code)
.audit-money-*/
audit/2026-09-29-*/

# Gated research PDFs live in PRIVATE storage (docs/research/RESEARCH_PLATFORM.md).
# Never commit them: this repository is public.
/FurlPay Stablecoin Report 2026.pdf
